   "body": "### Initial Checks\n\n- [x] I have searched Google & GitHub for similar requests and couldn't find anything\n- [x] I have read and followed [the docs](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/get-started/) and still think this feature is missing\n\n### Description\n\nDescription\n  On Windows 11 with Smart App Control turned on, `import pydantic` can fail because Windows\n  blocks the compiled pydantic-core extension:\n\n  ```\n  ImportError: DLL load failed while importing _pydantic_core: An Application Control policy\n  has blocked this file.\n  ```\n\n  The `.pyd` files in the Windows wheels carry no Authenticode signature. I checked every build\n  I had at hand, from 2.33.2 to 2.50.5, on cp312, cp313 and cp314:\n\n  ```powershell\n  PS> (Get-AuthenticodeSignature .\\pydantic_core\\_pydantic_core.cp313-win_amd64.pyd).Status\n  NotSigned\n  ```\n\n  ### Why this matters\n\n  Smart App Control first asks Microsoft's cloud service whether a file is known to be safe.\n  When the service can't make a confident prediction, Windows allows the file only if it has a\n  valid signature ([Microsoft\n  docs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/apps/develop/smart-app-control/overview)). So\n  an unsigned file with no verdict yet is blocked. Microsoft offers no per-app exception: an\n  affected user can only turn Smart App Control off for the whole machine. App Control for\n  Business policies that allow code by publisher can't allow an unsigned file either.\n\n  The block is not consistent, which makes it hard to reproduce. On a second Windows 11 25H2\n  machine with Smart App Control on, pydantic-core 2.50.5 and 2.46.5 loaded fine on Python\n  3.12, 3.13 and 3.14. That machine's Code Integrity log also showed the same unsigned file\n  being blocked once and allowed a few minutes later. This fits the reputation check: a new\n  release is most exposed before the cloud service has a verdict for its files. A signature\n  would remove that window.\n\n  Other projects that ship unsigned compiled files see the same reports, for example\n  python/mypy#21759 and astral-sh/uv#22869. uv now signs its own Windows binaries\n  (astral-sh/uv#10336).\n\n  ### Request\n\n  Sign the Windows `.pyd` files with a publicly trusted Authenticode certificate when the\n  wheels are built. Cloud signing services can sign from GitHub Actions without a private key\n  stored in the repository. The release workflow already publishes build provenance\n  attestations, but Windows does not read those; Smart App Control only checks Authenticode\n  signatures.\n\n - Windows 11 Pro 25H2, build 26200.9974\n  - Smart App Control: On during the tests, Off now\n  - Python 3.12.12 and 3.13.15 (uv-managed), 3.12.10 and 3.14.0 (python.org)\n  - pydantic 2.14.4 with pydantic-core 2.50.5, and pydantic 2.13.5 with pydantic-core 2.46.5: \n\n```\npydantic version: 2.14.4\npydantic-core version: 2.50.5\npydantic-core build: profile=release pgo=false\npython version: 3.13.15 (main, Sep  1 2026, 14:16:48) [MSC v.1944 64 bit (AMD64)]\nplatform: Windows-11-10.0.26200-SP0\n```\n\n### Affected Components\n\n- [ ] [Compatibility between releases](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/get-started/changelog/)\n- [ ] [Data validation/parsing](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/concepts/models/#basic-model-usage)\n- [ ] [Data serialization](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/concepts/serialization/) - `.model_dump()` and `.model_dump_json()`\n- [ ] [JSON Schema](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/concepts/json_schema/)\n- [ ] [Dataclasses](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/concepts/dataclasses/)\n- [ ] [Model Config](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/concepts/config/)\n- [ ] [Field Types](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/api/pydantic/types/) - adding or changing a particular data type\n- [ ] [Function validation decorator](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/concepts/validation_decorator/)\n- [ ] [Generic Models](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/concepts/models/#generic-models)\n- [ ] [Other Model behaviour](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/concepts/models/) - `model_construct()`, pickling, private attributes, ORM mode\n- [ ] [Plugins](https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/latest/integrations/dev-tools/mypy/) and integration with other tools - mypy, FastAPI, python-devtools, Hypothesis, VS Code, PyCharm, etc.",
