   "body": "Backport of #14410 to `v2.14-fixes`.\n\nCommit message description:\n\n```text\n(cherry picked from commit 2ebdaa0aec9638fdfd98f082233e7388266b49f7)\n\nBackport-of: #14410\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n```\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> The cherry-pick conflicted, and the conflicts were resolved by an agent. Review the resolutions carefully.\n\n<details><summary>Agent report</summary>\n\n## `.github/workflows/upload-previews.yml`\n\nThe PR is a CI-only change: it bumps `dawidd6/action-download-artifact` to v28. On `v2.14-fixes` the action was pinned to v24, because the earlier bump from v24 to v27 (#14177) was never backported. That made the context lines differ, which caused the conflict.\n\nThe conflict was resolved by pinning the action to v28 (`a92c7ae74cf1df8810783758581e485ac3aaa309`), the same pin as on `main`. This replaces the v24 pin, so #14177 doesn't need to be backported separately. The step's inputs (`workflow`, `commit`, ...) are the same on both branches.\n\nThe rest of the file is unchanged from `v2.14-fixes`. In particular, it keeps `python-version: '3.10'`, because the switch to 3.12 on `main` comes from #14250 (\"Drop support for Python 3.10\"), which isn't part of this PR.\n\n## Tests\n\nNo tests were run. The change only touches a GitHub Actions workflow pin, and no Python or Rust code was changed.\n\n</details>\n\nAgent run: https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/actions/runs/45673736808",
